  "solution": {
    "brief": "Wasp example 21: advancing into new topic series",
    "principle": "\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Tutorial 22 (wasp_22) directly continues the new topic series introduced in tutorial 21, confirming that tutorial 21 is the start of a new series focused on part-based, file-io, and multi-part aggregation workflows. Tutorial 21 is a direct prerequisite for tutorial 22.\n\nRelated insight: \n\nRelated insight: Tutorial 24 (wasp_24) continues the new topic series beyond tutorial 23, confirming the new series extends through at least tutorial 24. Tutorial 21 is an indirect prerequisite for tutorial 24 via tutorials 22 and 23. The series increasingly incorporates attribute-driven, graph-mapper, and field-driven aggregation techniques.\n\nRelated insight: \n\nRelated insight: Tutorial 25 (wasp_25) continues the new topic series beyond tutorial 24, confirming the series extends through at least tutorial 25. The series now incorporates iso-curve and gradient-visualization techniques alongside the established attribute-driven, field-driven, and multi-part aggregation workflows. Tutorial 21 remains the indirect prerequisite for tutorial 25 via tutorials 22, 23, and 24.\n\nRelated insight: Tutorial 26 (wasp_26) continues the new topic series beyond tutorial 25, confirming the series extends through at least tutorial 26. The series now incorporates contour-field as a new technique alongside the established iso-curve, gradient-visualization, attribute-driven, field-driven, and multi-part aggregation workflows. Tutorial 21 remains the indirect prerequisite for tutorial 26 via tutorials 22, 23, 24, and 25.\n\nRelated insight: Tutorial 27 (wasp_27) continues the new topic series beyond tutorial 26, confirming the series extends through at least tutorial 27. Tutorial 27 introduces or emphasizes stochastic techniques within the established constraint-based, multi-part, and discrete-aggregation workflows. Tutorial 21 remains the indirect prerequisite for tutorial 27 via tutorials 22, 23, 24, 25, and 26.\n\nRelated insight: Tutorial 33 (wasp_33) continues the constraints sub-series beyond tutorial 27, confirming the new topic series extends through at least tutorial 33. Tutorial 33 introduces export, DisCo, and connection-rules as new techniques within the established constraint-based, multi-part, and discrete-aggregation workflows. Tutorial 21 remains the indirect prerequisite for tutorial 33 via the chain of tutorials 22 through 32.",
